# =============================================================================
# Jiva Greens environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development:
#
#     cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Only this template is committed. `.env.local` and every other `.env*` file are
# gitignored. Never commit API keys, passwords, SMTP credentials, private tokens
# or production secrets.
#
# This file lists the variables the current codebase actually reads, and nothing
# else. The site is a static frontend: there is no backend of our own, no CMS
# and no database. Enquiry email is delivered by FormSubmit, a hosted service
# the browser posts to directly, so there are no SMTP credentials here either.
# Variables are added when the feature that needs them is built.
#
# Every value is read and validated in `config/env.ts`. Nothing else reads
# process.env directly.
#
# All four below are NEXT_PUBLIC_, which means they are inlined into the
# browser bundle at build time and are visible to anyone. Never put a secret in
# one.
# =============================================================================


# Which deployment this is: development | staging | production
#
# Two things depend on it.
#
# 1. Indexing. Any value other than "production" makes every page `noindex` and
#    serves a disallow-all robots.txt, so previews never appear in search
#    results. Unset or unrecognised values count as "development".
#
# 2. Page release. In production, `config/pageVisibility.ts` decides which pages
#    are reachable; a page switched off there returns the 404 page, including on
#    a direct URL. Development and staging ignore those flags and serve every
#    implemented page, so unreleased work stays reviewable internally.
#
# LAUNCH CHECKLIST: the live deployment must set this to "production", or the
# site will not be indexed and the page switchboard will not be enforced.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=development

# Canonical origin with no trailing slash. Drives canonical URLs, Open Graph
# URLs, the sitemap, robots.txt and structured data.
# Falls back to https://www.jivagreens.com when unset.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Number for the floating WhatsApp button and the WhatsApp actions on the
# Contact page and the enquiry form. Full international format, digits only, no
# "+" and no spaces: country code 91 followed by the 10-digit mobile, for
# example 91XXXXXXXXXX.
#
# Leave empty to hide every WhatsApp action. A value that is not 11 to 15 digits
# is treated as empty.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WHATSAPP_NUMBER=

# Where the enquiry form delivers, through FormSubmit (https://formsubmit.co).
# The form posts to https://formsubmit.co/ajax/<this value>.
#
# Two things can go here:
#
#   1. The recipient email address, for example enquiries@example.in. Simplest,
#      but this file is inlined into the browser bundle, so the address is
#      published on the page where scrapers can collect it.
#   2. The random token FormSubmit issues for that address. Preferred: it
#      delivers to the same inbox without naming it. To get one, submit the form
#      once with the address here, confirm the activation email FormSubmit
#      sends, and copy the token from your FormSubmit dashboard.
#
# FIRST USE: FormSubmit emails the address a one-time activation link. Until
# somebody clicks it, submissions are held rather than delivered.
#
# Leave empty and the form stops claiming anything was sent: it says online
# submission is not connected and offers email, phone and WhatsApp instead. A
# value that is neither an email address nor a token counts as empty.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FORMSUBMIT_EMAIL=
